[31m-## Structural Inferences[m
[31m-1. The "Shard-Locked" Persistence Model[m
[31m-   - Discovery: Critical security state (Beast Mode, Rapid Action Timers, Voice Sessions) resides exclusively in local Map objects.[m
[31m-   - Inference: The bot cannot scale beyond a single shard (~2,500 guilds) without a rewrite into Redis or centralized DB. Sharding will cause split-brain syndrome where security data is not shared between processes.[m
[31m-   - Risk: CRITICAL. Growth will eventually break security features.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-2. Event-Loop Blockade (The Monday Problem)[m
[31m-   - Discovery: scheduler.js performs O(N) sequential iterations through recruiters and audit logs on the main thread.[m
[31m-   - Belief: During the 00:05 UTC reset, the bot's event loop will block for 5-15 seconds.[m
[31m-   - Inference: Anti-Nuke protection is effectively "Off" during the reset window because the bot cannot process Discord events while the scheduler is crunching math.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-3. The "Permisiveness" Debt[m
[31m-   - Discovery: Widespread catch(() => {}) patterns across API calls.[m
[31m-   - Belief: Development choice for "uptime" over "correctness".[m
[31m-   - Inference: The bot provides false positives for success; staff may see "User Quarantined" while a 403 error left the executor active.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Security Logic Beliefs[m
[31m-4. Cold-Start Vulnerability[m
[31m-   - Discovery: createInviteTables and antinukeSystem.init are async and non-blocking in index.js.[m
[31m-   - Inference: 3-5 second window after startup where bot is online but unprotected; a nuke during startup bypasses logic as Maps haven't hydrated from antinuke_data.json.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-5. Identity Fragmentation[m
[31m-   - Discovery: Bot uses Discord IDs for some checks (Owner, Whitelist) but Role IDs for others (Region membership).[m
[31m-   - Inference: Role changes by server owners desync the bot's internal "truth". No automated reconciliation beyond basic scheduler checks.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Long-term Maintenance Risks[m
[31m-6. Transactional Void[m
[31m-   - Discovery: Zero SQL transactions (BEGIN/COMMIT) for multi-step operations (Promote -> Nickname -> DB Sync).[m
[31m-   - Inference: Database corruption is inevitable during high-concurrency periods (e.g., mass recruitment events).[m
